Upstream-Name: linux-legacy-oled-brightness
Upstream-Contact: Chris Xiong <chris@pineapple.cat>
Source: https://git.chrisoft.org/git/linux-legacy-oled-brightness.git
Comment: Upstream's repository (at a350d0e, 2026-03-28) has no license file
 and its README states no license; only the two new kernel files in its
 patch carry license headers.

Files: *
Copyright: 2026 Johannes Dahl <muusik@gmail.com>
License: MIT

Files: reference/*.html
Copyright: their sites and authors
License: none-stated
Comment: Saved copies of web pages (bug reports, forum threads, a Lenovo
 support note), kept for reference. Not in the binary package.

Files: upstream/linux-legacy-oled-brightness.patch
Copyright: 2025-2026 Chris Xiong
License: MIT and none-stated
Comment: Only its i915 part is applied, not its hunk for
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/Makefile. The two files it adds,
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_legacy_oled_brightness.c and .h, carry
 "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT" and "Copyright © 2025 Chris Xiong": MIT.
 Its changes to existing i915 files state no license of their own; those
 files are Linux's i915 under the licenses in their own headers (Makefile:
 GPL-2.0; intel_dp_aux_backlight.c and intel_display_types.h: MIT, copyright
 Intel Corporation and others). This package builds them from the
 linux-source package; it ships no other i915 source.

Files: patches/0002-module-firmware.patch
Copyright: 2026 Johannes Dahl <muusik@gmail.com>
License: MIT
Comment: Changes intel_dp_legacy_oled_brightness.c, which is MIT (above).

Files: upstream/gen_panel_prop.py
Copyright: 2025-2026 Chris Xiong
License: none-stated
Comment: The script carries no license header. Its tables are values from
 Lenovo's Windows "Intel OLED Panel Driver" for the ThinkPad X1 Yoga
 (PanelDriver.inf and PanelDriver.sys). The script itself is not in the
 binary package; its output is, as
 /usr/lib/firmware/intel_legacy_panel_data.bin.

